---
description: >-
  Classic-look sequence diagram where participants combine typed
  `@{ "type": ... }` stereotypes (boundary, control, database, entity)
  with the separate `as` keyword for the display alias, rather than an
  inline `alias` field in the config object as in the sibling
  "-inline-alias-in-config-object" fixture.
config:
  look: classic
  sequence:
    diagramMarginX: 50
    diagramMarginY: 10
---
sequenceDiagram
  participant API@{ "type" : "boundary" } as Public API
  participant Auth@{ "type" : "control" } as Auth Controller
  participant DB@{ "type" : "database" } as User Database
  participant Cache@{ "type" : "entity" } as Cache Layer
  API ->> Auth: Authenticate request
  Auth ->> DB: Query user
  DB -->> Auth: User data
  Auth ->> Cache: Store session
  Cache -->> Auth: Confirmed
  Auth -->> API: Token
